Suppose $X \to Z \to B$ are morphisms of algebraic spaces over $S$.
Given a scheme $T$ we can consider pairs $(a, b)$ where $a : T \to B$
is a morphism and $b : T \times_{a, B} Z \to X$ is a morphism over $Z$.
Picture
\begin{equation}
\label{equation-pairs}
\vcenter{
